# Urdu Deepfake Audio Detection

This repository contains the code, documentation, and reproducibility files for the project on privacy-preserving Urdu deepfake audio detection.

## Project summary

This project detects synthetic or spoofed Urdu speech using privacy-aware feature extraction and lightweight machine learning models. The research focuses on speaker-independent evaluation, robustness under noise, and efficient deployment.

## Main contributions

- Multi-tool synthetic speech dataset creation
- Speaker-independent training and evaluation
- Privacy-preserving feature-only pipeline
- Benchmarking of LightweightCNN, ECAPA-TDNN, and AASIST
- Robustness testing under noisy and compressed conditions

## Repository structure

- `src/` model and training code
- `data/` dataset metadata or allowed inputs
- `features/` extracted features only, not raw audio
- `results/` metrics, plots, and outputs
- `models/` saved checkpoints
- `notebooks/` experiments and analysis
- `reproducibility.md` run instructions and environment details
- `requirements.txt` dependency list
- `README.md` project overview

## Installation

```bash
git clone https://github.com/your-username/urdu-deepfake-detection.git
cd urdu-deepfake-detection
pip install -r requirements.txt
Training
python src/train.py
Evaluation
python src/evaluate.py
Expected outputs
•	Equal Error Rate
•	AUC score
•	inference time
•	robustness results
•	calibration or confusion plots
Privacy note
This repository stores extracted features and metadata instead of raw audio whenever possible to reduce privacy risk.
